/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · John chapters 11-15
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("john", [
{n:11, name:"Lazarus Raised", seal:{ref:"John 11:25",verse:"Jesus said unto her, I am the resurrection, and the life: he that believeth in me, though he were dead, yet shall he live:"},
 facts:["Did you know John 11:35, 'Jesus wept,' is the shortest verse in the KJV? It shows the Lord of life grieving at a friend's grave before He acts.","Did you know Lazarus had lain in the grave four days already when Jesus arrived (John 11:17)? By Jewish custom the soul was thought to linger three days, so the fourth day marked him as truly dead.","Did you know the miracle of Lazarus made the chief priests resolve not only to kill Jesus but Lazarus too (John 11:53, John 12:10)? His living body was evidence they could not answer."],
 questions:[
  {q:"Who was the sick man of Bethany in John 11?", options:["Lazarus","Bartimaeus","Nicodemus","Malchus"], a:0, ref:"John 11:1",verse:"Now a certain man was sick, named Lazarus, of Bethany, the town of Mary and her sister Martha.",
   insight:"The story begins with a real man's illness, not a parable. The miracle that follows happened to a named friend of Jesus."},
  {q:"Which Mary is named as the sister of Lazarus?", options:["The Mary who anointed the Lord with ointment and wiped His feet with her hair","The Mary who was the mother of James and Joses","Mary the mother of Jesus","Mary of Magdala only in Luke"], a:0, ref:"John 11:2",verse:"(It was that Mary which anointed the Lord with ointment, and wiped his feet with her hair, whose brother Lazarus was sick.)",
   insight:"John ties this Mary to her costly act of worship. The family was already known for deep devotion before the miracle came."},
  {q:"How long did Jesus remain where He was after hearing Lazarus was sick?", options:["Two days","One day","Seven days","Three days"], a:0, ref:"John 11:6",verse:"When he had heard therefore that he was sick, he abode two days still in the same place where he was.",
   insight:"Jesus delayed on purpose, out of love, not neglect. The wait let God's glory shine in a way a quicker healing could not."},
  {q:"What did the disciples fear about going back to Judea?", options:["The Jews of late sought to stone Jesus","A famine was spreading","The Romans blocked the roads","The passover was past"], a:0, ref:"John 11:8",verse:"His disciples say unto him, Master, the Jews of late sought to stone thee; and goest thou thither again?",
   insight:"Their fear was real and justified. Yet Jesus walked into danger for a friend, showing love that does not shrink from cost."},
  {q:"When Jesus said, 'Our friend Lazarus sleepeth,' what did He mean?", options:["Lazarus was dead","Lazarus was resting peacefully","Lazarus was only dreaming","Lazarus was unconscious from fever"], a:0, ref:"John 11:13",verse:"Howbeit Jesus spake of his death: but they thought that he had spoken of taking of rest in sleep.",
   insight:"The disciples missed the point because they heard a figure of speech literally. Jesus then spoke plainly: Lazarus is dead."},
  {q:"Which disciple said, 'Let us also go, that we may die with him'?", options:["Thomas, called Didymus","Peter","Andrew","Philip"], a:0, ref:"John 11:16",verse:"Then said Thomas, which is called Didymus, unto his fellowdisciples, Let us also go, that we may die with him.",
   insight:"Thomas is often remembered for doubt, but here he shows raw courage. His loyalty was real even when his understanding was dark."},
  {q:"How many days had Lazarus lain in the grave when Jesus arrived?", options:["Four days","Three days","Seven days","Two days"], a:0, ref:"John 11:17",verse:"Then when Jesus came, he found that he had lain in the grave four days already.",
   insight:"Four days removed every human explanation. The miracle would be undeniable, and God's power would stand alone."},
  {q:"How far was Bethany from Jerusalem?", options:["About fifteen furlongs","About two miles","About thirty furlongs","About six furlongs"], a:0, ref:"John 11:18",verse:"Now Bethany was nigh unto Jerusalem, about fifteen furlongs off:",
   insight:"Bethany sat close to Jerusalem, so the news spread fast. A public miracle in a public place forced a public decision about Jesus."},
  {q:"Who went out to meet Jesus first when she heard He was coming?", options:["Martha","Mary","Salome","Joanna"], a:0, ref:"John 11:20",verse:"Then Martha, as soon as she heard that Jesus was coming, went and met him: but Mary sat still in the house.",
   insight:"Martha ran to meet Him while Mary sat still in the house. Two sisters grieved differently, and Jesus met each one where she was."},
  {q:"What confession did Martha make to Jesus?", options:["I believe that thou art the Christ, the Son of God, which should come into the world","I believe thou art John the Baptist risen","I believe thou art Elias","I believe thou art a prophet sent by God"], a:0, ref:"John 11:27",verse:"She saith unto him, Yea, Lord: I believe that thou art the Christ, the Son of God, which should come into the world.",
   insight:"Martha's grief did not destroy her faith. She confessed Christ plainly, showing that sorrow and strong belief can live together."},
  {q:"What did Mary do when she came to where Jesus was?", options:["She fell down at His feet","She embraced His neck","She ran back to the house","She stood silent at a distance"], a:0, ref:"John 11:32",verse:"Then when Mary was come where Jesus was, and saw him, she fell down at his feet, saying unto him, Lord, if thou hadst been here, my brother had not died.",
   insight:"Mary's grief poured out at the same feet she had anointed. Worship and weeping came from the same love."},
  {q:"What question did Jesus ask at the grave?", options:["Where have ye laid him?","Why did ye not send sooner?","Who rolled away the stone?","What day did he die?"], a:0, ref:"John 11:34",verse:"And said, Where have ye laid him? They said unto him, Lord, come and see.",
   insight:"Jesus knew the answer, but He asked so the mourners would bring Him to the place of sorrow. He meets us where we bury our dead."},
  {q:"Which verse is the shortest verse in the KJV?", options:["Jesus wept.","Peace be still.","Ask, and receive.","Follow me."], a:0, ref:"John 11:35",verse:"Jesus wept.",
   insight:"Two words hold the truth that the Son of God felt human sorrow. Our griefs are not beneath Him."},
  {q:"With what words did Jesus call Lazarus from the tomb?", options:["Lazarus, come forth.","Lazarus, awake now.","Rise, Lazarus.","Come out, my friend."], a:0, ref:"John 11:43",verse:"And when he thus had spoken, he cried with a loud voice, Lazarus, come forth.",
   insight:"He called the dead man by name with a loud voice. His word carried life itself, not just comfort."},
  {q:"What command did Jesus give after Lazarus came out bound?", options:["Loose him, and let him go.","Carry him into the house.","Burn the graveclothes.","Tell no one this night."], a:0, ref:"John 11:44",verse:"And he that was dead came forth, bound hand and foot with graveclothes: and his face was bound about with a napkin. Jesus saith unto them, Loose him, and let him go.",
   insight:"Lazarus came out alive but still wrapped. Jesus sets people free fully, and He lets His people help unwrap one another."},
  {q:"What did Jesus say the sickness was for, not unto?", options:["For the glory of God","For the testing of Martha","For the shaming of the Pharisees","For the wealth of the priests"], a:0, ref:"John 11:4",verse:"When Jesus heard that, he said, This sickness is not unto death, but for the glory of God, that the Son of God might be glorified thereby.",
   insight:"Suffering can have a purpose beyond what the sufferer sees. This sickness existed so the Son of God would be glorified."},
  {q:"What did Martha say about her dead brother when Jesus ordered the stone taken away?", options:["Lord, by this time he stinketh: for he hath been dead four days.","Lord, the tomb is sealed too tightly.","Lord, the Romans guard the grave.","Lord, we have no spices to anoint him."], a:0, ref:"John 11:39",verse:"Jesus said, Take ye away the stone. Martha, the sister of him that was dead, saith unto him, Lord, by this time he stinketh: for he hath been dead four days.",
   insight:"Martha's practical mind shrank at the smell of decay. Jesus answered doubt with a reminder: believe, and you will see God's glory."},
  {q:"What did Caiaphas say was expedient for the people?", options:["That one man should die for the people, and that the whole nation perish not","That the Romans should be paid tribute","That Lazarus should be sent away quietly","That Jesus should be left alone to teach"], a:0, ref:"John 11:50",verse:"Nor consider that it is expedient for us, that one man should die for the people, and that the whole nation perish not.",
   insight:"Caiaphas meant cold politics, but God made him prophesy the gospel. Jesus would indeed die so the nation could live."},
  {q:"What did the leaders decide from that day forward?", options:["To put Jesus to death","To excommunicate Lazarus","To bribe the Romans for troops","To leave Jerusalem entirely"], a:0, ref:"John 11:53",verse:"Then from that day forth they took counsel together for to put him to death.",
   insight:"The greatest miracle in John's gospel hardened the council into murder. Light divides people: it does not merely comfort them."},
  {q:"To what city near the wilderness did Jesus withdraw?", options:["Ephraim","Capernaum","Nazareth","Lydda"], a:0, ref:"John 11:54",verse:"Jesus therefore walked no more openly among the Jews; but went thence unto a country near to the wilderness, into a city called Ephraim, and there continued with his disciples.",
   insight:"Jesus timed His own hour. He withdrew until the passover He chose, proving He went to the cross willingly, not by accident."}
 ]},
{n:12, name:"The King Comes", seal:{ref:"John 12:13",verse:"Took branches of palm trees, and went forth to meet him, and cried, Hosanna: Blessed is the King of Israel that cometh in the name of the Lord."},
 facts:["Did you know Mary's pound of spikenard cost three hundred pence, about a full year's wages for a laborer (John 12:3,5)? Her worship was extravagant because her love was.","Did you know the crowd's cry of 'Hosanna' came from the same word the leaders later heard at Lazarus's tomb (John 12:17,18)? The miracle drew the multitudes that hailed the King.","Did you know many chief rulers secretly believed on Jesus but would not confess Him, 'for they loved the praise of men more than the praise of God' (John 12:42,43)? Fear of people can bury true faith."],
 questions:[
  {q:"How many days before the passover did Jesus come to Bethany?", options:["Six days","Three days","Ten days","Forty days"], a:0, ref:"John 12:1",verse:"Then Jesus six days before the passover came to Bethany, where Lazarus was which had been dead, whom he raised from the dead.",
   insight:"Six days before the cross, Jesus went to the home He loved. The shadow of the cross fell across even this supper with friends."},
  {q:"With what did Mary anoint the feet of Jesus?", options:["A pound of ointment of spikenard, very costly","A flask of olive oil","A box of frankincense","A bottle of myrrh and aloes"], a:0, ref:"John 12:3",verse:"Then took Mary a pound of ointment of spikenard, very costly, and anointed the feet of Jesus, and wiped his feet with her hair: and the house was filled with the odour of the ointment.",
   insight:"She poured out about a year's wages on His feet. True worship is costly, and Jesus accepted it as fitting."},
  {q:"For how much did Judas say the ointment could have been sold?", options:["Three hundred pence","Thirty pieces of silver","One hundred denarii","Fifty shekels"], a:0, ref:"John 12:5",verse:"Why was not this ointment sold for three hundred pence, and given to the poor?",
   insight:"Judas valued the ointment in coins but not in worship. A heart set on money cannot read an act of love."},
  {q:"Why did Judas object to the anointing?", options:["He was a thief and had the bag","He truly cared for the poor","He had promised it to the temple","He feared the Romans would tax it"], a:0, ref:"John 12:6",verse:"This he said, not that he cared for the poor; but because he was a thief, and had the bag, and bare what was put therein.",
   insight:"John exposes Judas's motive plainly. His complaint wore the mask of charity, but greed stood behind it."},
  {q:"How did Jesus explain Mary's act?", options:["Against the day of my burying hath she kept this","For the dedication of the new temple","For the healing of the sick poor","For the honor of her brother Lazarus"], a:0, ref:"John 12:7",verse:"Then said Jesus, Let her alone: against the day of my burying hath she kept this.",
   insight:"Mary anointed Him before His death without knowing it. Devotion done in love often carries a meaning we only see later."},
  {q:"Why did the chief priests plan to kill Lazarus as well?", options:["By reason of him many of the Jews went away and believed on Jesus","He had stolen from the temple treasury","He was plotting with the Romans","He refused to pay the temple tax"], a:0, ref:"John 12:11",verse:"Because that by reason of him many of the Jews went away, and believed on Jesus.",
   insight:"Lazarus was guilty of nothing but being raised. Living evidence of God's work still draws the world's hostility."},
  {q:"What branches did the people take to meet Jesus?", options:["Branches of palm trees","Branches of olive trees","Branches of fig trees","Branches of cedars"], a:0, ref:"John 12:13",verse:"Took branches of palm trees, and went forth to meet him, and cried, Hosanna: Blessed is the King of Israel that cometh in the name of the Lord.",
   insight:"Palm branches were symbols of victory and kingship. The crowd greeted Jesus as the King of Israel, and they were right."},
  {q:"What animal did Jesus sit on when He entered Jerusalem?", options:["A young ass","A white horse","A mule from Egypt","A camel from Bethany"], a:0, ref:"John 12:14",verse:"And Jesus, when he had found a young ass, sat thereon; as it is written,",
   insight:"A king riding a donkey's colt proclaimed peace, not war. Jesus came as the promised King in the exact manner prophecy described."},
  {q:"What prophecy was quoted about the coming King?", options:["Fear not, daughter of Sion: behold, thy King cometh, sitting on an ass's colt","Rejoice greatly, O daughter of Babylon","Behold, a virgin shall conceive","The sceptre shall not depart from Judah"], a:0, ref:"John 12:15",verse:"Fear not, daughter of Sion: behold, thy King cometh, sitting on an ass’s colt.",
   insight:"The entry fulfilled Zechariah's prophecy line by line. Scripture's details are not decoration; they are God's signature."},
  {q:"When did the disciples understand the meaning of the entry?", options:["When Jesus was glorified","The next morning","After the passover supper","When Peter denied Him"], a:0, ref:"John 12:16",verse:"These things understood not his disciples at the first: but when Jesus was glorified, then remembered they that these things were written of him, and that they had done these things unto him.",
   insight:"Understanding often comes after the event, not during it. They remembered Scripture's meaning once the resurrection lit it up."},
  {q:"Why did the crowds come out to meet Jesus that day?", options:["They heard He had raised Lazarus from the dead","They wanted bread and fish again","They sought to make Him king by force","They came for the passover lambs"], a:0, ref:"John 12:18",verse:"For this cause the people also met him, for that they heard that he had done this miracle.",
   insight:"The miracle at Bethany was the magnet. One public resurrection convinced multitudes faster than a thousand sermons."},
  {q:"What did the Pharisees say to one another in frustration?", options:["Perceive ye how ye prevail nothing? behold, the world is gone after him.","We must arrest Him this very night.","Let us ask the Romans for soldiers.","We should praise His mighty works."], a:0, ref:"John 12:19",verse:"The Pharisees therefore said among themselves, Perceive ye how ye prevail nothing? behold, the world is gone after him.",
   insight:"Their own words announced their defeat. The more they opposed Him, the more the world followed Him."},
  {q:"Who asked Philip for an audience with Jesus?", options:["Certain Greeks","Certain Romans","Certain Samaritans","Certain priests"], a:0, ref:"John 12:20",verse:"And there were certain Greeks among them that came up to worship at the feast:",
   insight:"Greeks seeking Jesus signaled that His hour had come. The gospel would not stay inside Israel; it was about to reach the nations."},
  {q:"What did the Greeks say to Philip?", options:["Sir, we would see Jesus.","Sir, where is the King?","Sir, heal our brother.","Sir, pay the tribute for us."], a:0, ref:"John 12:21",verse:"The same came therefore to Philip, which was of Bethsaida of Galilee, and desired him, saying, Sir, we would see Jesus.",
   insight:"Four words carried a world's longing. Whoever truly seeks to see Jesus still finds Him."},
  {q:"What did Jesus say about a corn of wheat?", options:["Except it fall into the ground and die, it abideth alone: but if it die, it bringeth forth much fruit","If it is ground into flour it feeds many","If it is planted in winter it yields nothing","If it is kept in the barn it stays safe forever"], a:0, ref:"John 12:24",verse:"Verily, verily, I say unto you, Except a corn of wheat fall into the ground and die, it abideth alone: but if it die, it bringeth forth much fruit.",
   insight:"Death comes before harvest. Jesus explained His own cross as the seed from which eternal life would grow."},
  {q:"What did Jesus pray when His soul was troubled?", options:["Father, glorify thy name.","Father, save me from this hour.","Father, send down fire.","Father, strike my enemies."], a:0, ref:"John 12:28",verse:"Father, glorify thy name. Then came there a voice from heaven, saying, I have both glorified it, and will glorify it again.",
   insight:"He refused to ask for escape and asked for glory instead. His whole soul bent toward the Father's name, not His own comfort."},
  {q:"What did the bystanders think the voice from heaven was?", options:["Some said it thundered; others said an angel spake to Him","All agreed it was thunder","All agreed it was an earthquake","Some said it was the wind"], a:0, ref:"John 12:29",verse:"The people therefore, that stood by, and heard it, said that it thundered: others said, An angel spake to him.",
   insight:"The same voice sounded different to different hearts. How we hear God depends on the ears we bring."},
  {q:"For whose sake did Jesus say the heavenly voice came?", options:["For your sakes, not His own","For the Greeks only","For the chief priests","For the Roman soldiers"], a:0, ref:"John 12:30",verse:"Jesus answered and said, This voice came not because of me, but for your sakes.",
   insight:"Jesus did not need the voice; the crowd did. God speaks for the sake of those who stand by and need to believe."},
  {q:"Why did many believing chief rulers refuse to confess Jesus?", options:["Lest they should be put out of the synagogue","Because they doubted the resurrection","Because they feared the Romans more","Because they loved their riches most"], a:0, ref:"John 12:42",verse:"Nevertheless among the chief rulers also many believed on him; but because of the Pharisees they did not confess him, lest they should be put out of the synagogue:",
   insight:"They believed but stayed silent from fear. A faith that will not confess is a faith that will not grow."},
  {q:"What reason did John give for their silence?", options:["They loved the praise of men more than the praise of God","They hated the poor and needy","They loved the temple gold","They feared losing their inheritances"], a:0, ref:"John 12:43",verse:"For they loved the praise of men more than the praise of God.",
   insight:"The praise of men is a poor master. It keeps silent the very faith that could save."}
 ]},
{n:13, name:"The Basin and the Betrayer", seal:{ref:"John 13:34",verse:"A new commandment I give unto you, That ye love one another; as I have loved you, that ye also love one another."},
 facts:["Did you know Jesus washed the feet of Judas too, knowing he would betray Him (John 13:11)? The Lord served even the man He knew was lost.","Did you know the disciple leaning on Jesus's bosom at supper was the one 'whom Jesus loved' (John 13:23)? Many believe this was John himself, who wrote these very words.","Did you know Jesus named the betrayer by giving him the dipped sop, and Judas left immediately into the night (John 13:26,30)? 'It was night' marks one of the darkest exits in Scripture."],
 questions:[
  {q:"When did the foot washing happen?", options:["Before the feast of the passover","After the resurrection morning","During the feast of tabernacles","At the feast of dedication"], a:0, ref:"John 13:1",verse:"Now before the feast of the passover, when Jesus knew that his hour was come that he should depart out of this world unto the Father, having loved his own which were in the world, he loved them unto the end.",
   insight:"Hours before the cross, Jesus chose to serve. His last evening was shaped by love, not by fear of what was coming."},
  {q:"What did Jesus lay aside and gird Himself with?", options:["His garments, and a towel","His sandals, and a cloak","His staff, and a girdle","His money, and a scrip"], a:0, ref:"John 13:4",verse:"He riseth from supper, and laid aside his garments; and took a towel, and girded himself.",
   insight:"The Lord of all dressed like a servant. He did not merely talk about humility; He tied it around His waist."},
  {q:"What did Peter first say when Jesus came to wash his feet?", options:["Lord, dost thou wash my feet?","Master, wash my hands first.","Rabbi, this is not fitting.","Teacher, let another do it."], a:0, ref:"John 13:6",verse:"Then cometh he to Simon Peter: and Peter saith unto him, Lord, dost thou wash my feet?",
   insight:"Peter's objection sounded like reverence, but it was really resistance. Love must let the Lord serve us His way."},
  {q:"What warning did Jesus give Peter?", options:["If I wash thee not, thou hast no part with me.","If thou question me, thou art none of mine.","If thou refuse me, thou art cut off.","If thou doubt me, thou hast no faith."], a:0, ref:"John 13:8",verse:"Peter saith unto him, Thou shalt never wash my feet. Jesus answered him, If I wash thee not, thou hast no part with me.",
   insight:"Refusing His cleansing keeps us from having any part with Him. We must receive His work before we can share His life."},
  {q:"What did Peter then ask for?", options:["Not my feet only, but also my hands and my head.","Wash me seven times over.","Wash the whole company first.","Wash me in the Jordan river."], a:0, ref:"John 13:9",verse:"Simon Peter saith unto him, Lord, not my feet only, but also my hands and my head.",
   insight:"Peter swung from refusal to excess. Once he saw the need, he wanted everything cleansed, which was exactly right."},
  {q:"Why did Jesus say, 'Ye are not all clean'?", options:["He knew who should betray Him","Judas had missed the passover","Thomas had touched the bread","Peter had doubted the supper"], a:0, ref:"John 13:11",verse:"For he knew who should betray him; therefore said he, Ye are not all clean.",
   insight:"Outward washing cannot reach an inward traitor. Ritual without a true heart leaves a man unclean."},
  {q:"What did Jesus say the disciples ought to do for one another?", options:["Wash one another's feet","Pay one another's debts","Share one another's houses","Forgive one another's taxes"], a:0, ref:"John 13:14",verse:"If I then, your Lord and Master, have washed your feet; ye also ought to wash one another’s feet.",
   insight:"The Master set the pattern in a basin of water. Greatness in His kingdom is measured by lowly service to others."},
  {q:"What saying did Jesus give about servants?", options:["The servant is not greater than his lord","The servant is equal to his lord","The servant outranks his master","The servant need not obey his lord"], a:0, ref:"John 13:16",verse:"Verily, verily, I say unto you, The servant is not greater than his lord; neither he that is sent greater than he that sent him.",
   insight:"If the Lord washed feet, no follower can claim the task is beneath him. Our rank never exempts us from service."},
  {q:"What did Jesus promise to those who know and do these things?", options:["Happy are ye if ye do them.","Rich are ye if ye do them.","Great are ye if ye do them.","Famous are ye if ye do them."], a:0, ref:"John 13:17",verse:"If ye know these things, happy are ye if ye do them.",
   insight:"Knowing is not enough; the blessing falls on the doing. Happiness follows obedience, not information."},
  {q:"Why did Jesus say He told them about the betrayal beforehand?", options:["Now I tell you before it come, that, when it is come to pass, ye may believe that I am he.","Now I tell you so ye may flee from Jerusalem.","Now I tell you so ye may warn the priests.","Now I tell you so ye may hide the money bag."], a:0, ref:"John 13:19",verse:"Now I tell you before it come, that, when it is come to pass, ye may believe that I am he.",
   insight:"He told them before it happened so the betrayal itself would become proof of who He is. Foretold events turn into foundations of faith."},
  {q:"Who was leaning on Jesus's bosom at supper?", options:["One of His disciples, whom Jesus loved","Thomas, called Didymus","Andrew, the brother of Peter","Matthew, the publican"], a:0, ref:"John 13:23",verse:"Now there was leaning on Jesus’ bosom one of his disciples, whom Jesus loved.",
   insight:"This beloved disciple rested close to Jesus's heart. Nearness to Christ is open to all who love Him."},
  {q:"How did Jesus identify the one who would betray Him?", options:["To whom I shall give a sop, when I have dipped it","Whoever rises from the table first","Whoever takes the last cup","Whoever asks for the bread"], a:0, ref:"John 13:26",verse:"Jesus answered, He it is, to whom I shall give a sop, when I have dipped it. And when he had dipped the sop, he gave it to Judas Iscariot, the son of Simon.",
   insight:"A common table gesture became the sign of treason. Betrayal often hides inside ordinary fellowship."},
  {q:"Who received the dipped sop?", options:["Judas Iscariot, the son of Simon","Thomas, called Didymus","Philip of Bethsaida","Nathanael of Cana"], a:0, ref:"John 13:26",verse:"Jesus answered, He it is, to whom I shall give a sop, when I have dipped it. And when he had dipped the sop, he gave it to Judas Iscariot, the son of Simon.",
   insight:"Jesus gave the sop to Judas as a final mark of love and warning. Even at the last, grace reached toward the betrayer."},
  {q:"What did Jesus tell Judas after Satan entered him?", options:["That thou doest, do quickly.","Go, and betray me openly.","Flee, and hide thyself.","Repent, and be restored."], a:0, ref:"John 13:27",verse:"And after the sop Satan entered into him. Then said Jesus unto him, That thou doest, do quickly.",
   insight:"Jesus remained in command even over the betrayal. Darkness moved only when the Light permitted it."},
  {q:"What did the other disciples think Jesus meant?", options:["Buy things needed for the feast, or give something to the poor","Go and call the Romans","Fetch more wine for the table","Prepare a room for prayer"], a:0, ref:"John 13:29",verse:"For some of them thought, because Judas had the bag, that Jesus had said unto him, Buy those things that we have need of against the feast; or, that he should give something to the poor.",
   insight:"They were blind to the treason at their own table. Evil can work beside us while we think only of ordinary errands."},
  {q:"How does John describe the moment Judas went out?", options:["And it was night.","And it was raining.","And it was silent.","And it was the third hour."], a:0, ref:"John 13:30",verse:"He then having received the sop went immediately out: and it was night.",
   insight:"Three words carry terrible weight. When a man walks away from Christ, the darkness is not just around him but in him."},
  {q:"What new commandment did Jesus give?", options:["That ye love one another, as I have loved you.","That ye fast twice in the week.","That ye tithe of all ye possess.","That ye build a new temple."], a:0, ref:"John 13:34",verse:"A new commandment I give unto you, That ye love one another; as I have loved you, that ye also love one another.",
   insight:"The standard is not 'as you love yourself' but 'as I have loved you.' Christ's own love is the measure of ours."},
  {q:"How will all men know we are His disciples?", options:["If ye have love one to another.","If ye keep the sabbaths strictly.","If ye speak with tongues.","If ye wear the priestly robes."], a:0, ref:"John 13:35",verse:"By this shall all men know that ye are my disciples, if ye have love one to another.",
   insight:"The badge of discipleship is not dress or ritual but love. The world reads our love as proof of our Lord."},
  {q:"What did Jesus say when Peter asked where He was going?", options:["Whither I go, thou canst not follow me now; but thou shalt follow me afterwards.","I go to Galilee to fish.","I go to the temple to pray.","I go alone to the wilderness."], a:0, ref:"John 13:36",verse:"Simon Peter said unto him, Lord, whither goest thou? Jesus answered him, Whither I go, thou canst not follow me now; but thou shalt follow me afterwards.",
   insight:"Peter's path would lead through denial first. Following Christ comes in God's timing, not in our eagerness."},
  {q:"What did Jesus predict Peter would do before the cock crowed?", options:["Deny Him thrice.","Flee to Egypt.","Betray Him for silver.","Sleep in the garden."], a:0, ref:"John 13:38",verse:"Jesus answered him, Wilt thou lay down thy life for my sake? Verily, verily, I say unto thee, The cock shall not crow, till thou hast denied me thrice.",
   insight:"Jesus knew the boast and the fall before either happened. His warning was both true and tender, given to save Peter, not shame him."}
 ]},
{n:14, name:"The Way, the Truth, the Life", seal:{ref:"John 14:6",verse:"Jesus saith unto him, I am the way, the truth, and the life: no man cometh unto the Father, but by me."},
 facts:["Did you know Jesus said His Father's house has 'many mansions' (John 14:2)? He went to prepare a place, which is why Christians speak of heaven as home.","Did you know the Comforter Jesus promised is the Spirit of truth, whom the world cannot receive but who would dwell in believers (John 14:16,17)? The Holy Spirit is a Person, not a force.","Did you know Jesus gave His peace as a gift, 'not as the world giveth' (John 14:27)? The world's peace depends on circumstances; His holds when trouble comes."],
 questions:[
  {q:"How does John 14 open?", options:["Let not your heart be troubled: ye believe in God, believe also in me.","Fear not, little flock.","Be of good cheer, I have overcome.","Come unto me, all ye that labor."], a:0, ref:"John 14:1",verse:"Let not your heart be troubled: ye believe in God, believe also in me.",
   insight:"Jesus spoke these words on the night of His betrayal. His comfort to troubled hearts began before the trouble arrived."},
  {q:"What is in the Father's house?", options:["Many mansions","Twelve gates of pearl","A sea of glass","Seven golden lamps"], a:0, ref:"John 14:2",verse:"In my Father’s house are many mansions: if it were not so, I would have told you. I go to prepare a place for you.",
   insight:"There is room for all who come. Heaven is not crowded or closed; Jesus Himself went ahead to prepare our place."},
  {q:"What did Jesus promise to do after preparing a place?", options:["I will come again, and receive you unto myself","I will send fire from heaven","I will write your names in stone","I will build a new temple"], a:0, ref:"John 14:3",verse:"And if I go and prepare a place for you, I will come again, and receive you unto myself; that where I am, there ye may be also.",
   insight:"He did not leave us to find our own way home. He will return in person to bring His people to Himself."},
  {q:"What did Thomas ask?", options:["Lord, we know not whither thou goest; and how can we know the way?","Lord, show us a sign from heaven.","Lord, when wilt thou restore the kingdom?","Lord, who is the greatest among us?"], a:0, ref:"John 14:5",verse:"Thomas saith unto him, Lord, we know not whither thou goest; and how can we know the way?",
   insight:"Thomas asked an honest question and received the greatest answer ever given about how to reach God."},
  {q:"What did Jesus say about Himself?", options:["I am the way, the truth, and the life: no man cometh unto the Father, but by me.","I am the door, and the shepherd, and the vine.","I am the light, and the salt, and the bread.","I am the root, and the branch, and the star."], a:0, ref:"John 14:6",verse:"Jesus saith unto him, I am the way, the truth, and the life: no man cometh unto the Father, but by me.",
   insight:"He claimed to be the only road to the Father, not one road among many. The claim is either true for all or false for all."},
  {q:"What did Jesus tell Philip about seeing Him?", options:["He that hath seen me hath seen the Father.","He that hath seen me hath seen an angel.","He that hath seen me needeth no faith.","He that hath seen me shall see Moses."], a:0, ref:"John 14:9",verse:"Jesus saith unto him, Have I been so long time with you, and yet hast thou not known me, Philip? he that hath seen me hath seen the Father; and how sayest thou then, Shew us the Father?",
   insight:"To look at Jesus is to look at the Father's heart. God is not hidden behind Christ; He is revealed in Him."},
  {q:"What did Jesus say believers would do?", options:["The works that I do shall he do also; and greater works than these.","They shall judge the twelve tribes.","They shall raise the temple in three days.","They shall turn the sea into blood."], a:0, ref:"John 14:12",verse:"Verily, verily, I say unto you, He that believeth on me, the works that I do shall he do also; and greater works than these shall he do; because I go unto my Father.",
   insight:"Because He went to the Father, His work would multiply through His people. Greater in reach, not greater in power."},
  {q:"What did Jesus promise about asking in His name?", options:["Whatsoever ye shall ask in my name, that will I do.","Whatever ye ask for riches shall be doubled.","Whatever ye ask in secret shall be hidden.","Whatever ye ask of men shall be granted."], a:0, ref:"John 14:13",verse:"And whatsoever ye shall ask in my name, that will I do, that the Father may be glorified in the Son.",
   insight:"Praying in His name means praying in line with who He is. Such prayer aims at the Father's glory, not our greed."},
  {q:"What is the proof of loving Jesus?", options:["If ye love me, keep my commandments.","If ye love me, build me a house.","If ye love me, fast forty days.","If ye love me, sell all thou hast."], a:0, ref:"John 14:15",verse:"If ye love me, keep my commandments.",
   insight:"Love is measured by obedience, not by feeling. Keeping His word is how the heart proves its love."},
  {q:"Whom did Jesus promise to pray the Father to send?", options:["Another Comforter, to abide with them forever","Another prophet, to teach them law","Another king, to rule the nations","Another angel, to guard their way"], a:0, ref:"John 14:16",verse:"And I will pray the Father, and he shall give you another Comforter, that he may abide with you for ever;",
   insight:"'Another' means one like Jesus Himself. The Comforter would take His place beside them and never leave."},
  {q:"What is the Comforter called?", options:["The Spirit of truth","The Spirit of power","The Spirit of fire","The Spirit of wisdom"], a:0, ref:"John 14:17",verse:"Even the Spirit of truth; whom the world cannot receive, because it seeth him not, neither knoweth him: but ye know him; for he dwelleth with you, and shall be in you.",
   insight:"The world cannot receive Him because it cannot see Him. But believers know Him, for He dwells with them and in them."},
  {q:"What promise did Jesus make about leaving them?", options:["I will not leave you comfortless: I will come to you.","I will leave you to your own strength.","I will hide myself for forty years.","I will send you back to your nets."], a:0, ref:"John 14:18",verse:"I will not leave you comfortless: I will come to you.",
   insight:"He would not abandon them like orphans. His going would not mean their loneliness."},
  {q:"Who is it that truly loves Jesus?", options:["He that hath my commandments, and keepeth them.","He that sings the loudest hymns.","He that gives the largest offerings.","He that fasts the longest fasts."], a:0, ref:"John 14:21",verse:"He that hath my commandments, and keepeth them, he it is that loveth me: and he that loveth me shall be loved of my Father, and I will love him, and will manifest myself to him.",
   insight:"Love is not proved by noise or gifts but by keeping His word. To such a one Jesus promises to manifest Himself."},
  {q:"Which Judas asked why Jesus would manifest Himself to them and not to the world?", options:["Judas, not Iscariot","Judas Iscariot, son of Simon","Judas the brother of James the Less","Judas of Galilee"], a:0, ref:"John 14:22",verse:"Judas saith unto him, not Iscariot, Lord, how is it that thou wilt manifest thyself unto us, and not unto the world?",
   insight:"John carefully notes this was the other Judas. The traitor was already gone into the night; this question came from a faithful heart."},
  {q:"What did Jesus promise the one who loves Him and keeps His words?", options:["My Father will love him, and we will come unto him, and make our abode with him.","He shall sit on my throne forever.","He shall never taste of death.","He shall rule over ten cities."], a:0, ref:"John 14:23",verse:"Jesus answered and said unto him, If a man love me, he will keep my words: and my Father will love him, and we will come unto him, and make our abode with him.",
   insight:"Obedient love opens the door to God's own presence. The Father and Son make their home in the heart that keeps His word."},
  {q:"What would the Comforter do for the disciples?", options:["Teach them all things, and bring all things to their remembrance.","Write new laws on tables of stone.","Judge the nations at the last day.","Build the church in Jerusalem."], a:0, ref:"John 14:26",verse:"But the Comforter, which is the Holy Ghost, whom the Father will send in my name, he shall teach you all things, and bring all things to your remembrance, whatsoever I have said unto you.",
   insight:"The Spirit would not bring a different message but would recall Christ's own words. That is why we can trust the gospel record."},
  {q:"What kind of peace did Jesus leave them?", options:["My peace, not as the world giveth.","The peace of the Roman empire.","The peace of a quiet conscience only.","The peace of riches and plenty."], a:0, ref:"John 14:27",verse:"Peace I leave with you, my peace I give unto you: not as the world giveth, give I unto you. Let not your heart be troubled, neither let it be afraid.",
   insight:"The world's peace breaks when trouble comes. His peace holds inside trouble, which is why He could give it on betrayal night."},
  {q:"Why did Jesus say they should rejoice at His going to the Father?", options:["For my Father is greater than I.","For the temple would be destroyed.","For the Romans would depart.","For the law would be fulfilled."], a:0, ref:"John 14:28",verse:"Ye have heard how I said unto you, I go away, and come again unto you. If ye loved me, ye would rejoice, because I said, I go unto the Father: for my Father is greater than I.",
   insight:"His return to the Father was His exaltation, not His defeat. Love rejoices when the beloved is glorified."},
  {q:"What did Jesus say about the prince of this world?", options:["He cometh, and hath nothing in me.","He is cast down by my angels.","He flees at my command.","He serves my Father's will."], a:0, ref:"John 14:30",verse:"Hereafter I will not talk much with you: for the prince of this world cometh, and hath nothing in me.",
   insight:"Satan had no claim on Jesus, no sin to accuse Him of. The cross would be no victory for darkness but its defeat."},
  {q:"How does the chapter end?", options:["Arise, let us go hence.","Watch and pray with me.","Sleep now, and take rest.","Depart, for it is finished."], a:0, ref:"John 14:31",verse:"But that the world may know that I love the Father; and as the Father gave me commandment, even so I do. Arise, let us go hence.",
   insight:"After the sweetest comfort ever spoken, Jesus rose to face the betrayer. Peace in the heart does not mean shrinking from the path."}
 ]},
{n:15, name:"The True Vine", seal:{ref:"John 15:5",verse:"I am the vine, ye are the branches: He that abideth in me, and I in him, the same bringeth forth much fruit: for without me ye can do nothing."},
 facts:["Did you know Jesus called Himself 'the true vine' and His Father 'the husbandman,' the gardener (John 15:1)? The Father tends believers the way a vinedresser tends branches, for fruit.","Did you know 'Greater love hath no man than this, that a man lay down his life for his friends' (John 15:13)? Jesus spoke these words hours before laying down His own life.","Did you know Jesus called His disciples friends, not servants, because He told them everything He heard from the Father (John 15:15)? He brings His followers into His confidence."],
 questions:[
  {q:"Who did Jesus say is the husbandman of the true vine?", options:["My Father","The chief priests","The keepers of the temple","The apostles"], a:0, ref:"John 15:1",verse:"I am the true vine, and my Father is the husbandman.",
   insight:"The Father is the gardener who tends the vine. Our fruitfulness is His careful work, not our own striving."},
  {q:"What happens to every branch in Christ that bears no fruit?", options:["He taketh it away.","He leaves it alone.","He grafts it again.","He waters it more."], a:0, ref:"John 15:2",verse:"Every branch in me that beareth not fruit he taketh away: and every branch that beareth fruit, he purgeth it, that it may bring forth more fruit.",
   insight:"A fruitless profession is cut off. Bearing fruit is not optional decoration; it is the evidence of true union with Christ."},
  {q:"What does the Father do to the branch that bears fruit?", options:["He purgeth it, that it may bring forth more fruit.","He lets it grow wild.","He transplants it elsewhere.","He hides it from the sun."], a:0, ref:"John 15:2",verse:"Every branch in me that beareth not fruit he taketh away: and every branch that beareth fruit, he purgeth it, that it may bring forth more fruit.",
   insight:"Pruning hurts, but its purpose is more fruit, not less. God's discipline is always aimed at increase."},
  {q:"What command sums up the vine teaching?", options:["Abide in me, and I in you.","Work harder for the harvest.","Seek the branches of others.","Water the roots daily."], a:0, ref:"John 15:4",verse:"Abide in me, and I in you. As the branch cannot bear fruit of itself, except it abide in the vine; no more can ye, except ye abide in me.",
   insight:"The branch's only job is to stay joined to the vine. Fruit comes from remaining, not from straining."},
  {q:"What did Jesus say we can do without Him?", options:["Nothing.","Little.","Much, with effort.","Some good works."], a:0, ref:"John 15:5",verse:"I am the vine, ye are the branches: He that abideth in me, and I in him, the same bringeth forth much fruit: for without me ye can do nothing.",
   insight:"'Nothing' leaves no room for boasting. Apart from Christ, all our labor in spiritual things comes to zero."},
  {q:"What happens to the branch that abides not in Christ?", options:["He is cast forth, withered, and burned.","He is planted in a new field.","He is kept for another season.","He is sold to the merchants."], a:0, ref:"John 15:6",verse:"If a man abide not in me, he is cast forth as a branch, and is withered; and men gather them, and cast them into the fire, and they are burned.",
   insight:"Separation from Christ ends in ruin. The picture is severe because the reality is severe."},
  {q:"What promise is given to those who abide in Christ?", options:["Ye shall ask what ye will, and it shall be done unto you.","Ye shall never know sorrow.","Ye shall rule over the nations.","Ye shall be free from all enemies."], a:0, ref:"John 15:7",verse:"If ye abide in me, and my words abide in you, ye shall ask what ye will, and it shall be done unto you.",
   insight:"When His words live in us, our desires align with His. Then our asking carries the weight of His own will."},
  {q:"How is the Father glorified?", options:["That ye bear much fruit; so shall ye be my disciples.","That ye build a great temple.","That ye offer many sacrifices.","That ye keep the feasts yearly."], a:0, ref:"John 15:8",verse:"Herein is my Father glorified, that ye bear much fruit; so shall ye be my disciples.",
   insight:"God is glorified not by our busyness but by our fruitfulness. Much fruit proves true discipleship."},
  {q:"What did Jesus urge them to continue in?", options:["Continue ye in my love.","Continue ye in the law.","Continue ye in the temple.","Continue ye in the feast."], a:0, ref:"John 15:9",verse:"As the Father hath loved me, so have I loved you: continue ye in my love.",
   insight:"His love is a place to remain in, not a feeling to chase. He invites us to stay where His love already rests."},
  {q:"How do we abide in His love?", options:["If ye keep my commandments, ye shall abide in my love.","If ye fast often, ye shall abide.","If ye give alms daily, ye shall abide.","If ye pray all night, ye shall abide."], a:0, ref:"John 15:10",verse:"If ye keep my commandments, ye shall abide in my love; even as I have kept my Father’s commandments, and abide in his love.",
   insight:"Obedience is the path into the enjoyment of His love. Even Christ kept His Father's commandments as our example."},
  {q:"Why did Jesus speak these things to them?", options:["That my joy might remain in you, and that your joy might be full.","That ye might fear the coming judgment.","That ye might know the end of the world.","That ye might escape the Romans."], a:0, ref:"John 15:11",verse:"These things have I spoken unto you, that my joy might remain in you, and that your joy might be full.",
   insight:"His aim was their full joy, not their dread. Abiding in Christ is the way to a joy that nothing can empty."},
  {q:"What is His commandment in this chapter?", options:["That ye love one another, as I have loved you.","That ye hate the works of darkness.","That ye judge righteous judgment.","That ye tithe mint and rue."], a:0, ref:"John 15:12",verse:"This is my commandment, That ye love one another, as I have loved you.",
   insight:"The measure is His own love for us. We love others the way He has loved us, to the uttermost."},
  {q:"What is the greatest love?", options:["That a man lay down his life for his friends.","That a man give all his goods to the poor.","That a man travel to the ends of the earth.","That a man fast forty days and nights."], a:0, ref:"John 15:13",verse:"Greater love hath no man than this, that a man lay down his life for his friends.",
   insight:"Jesus spoke this hours before the cross. He did not only teach the greatest love; He was about to show it."},
  {q:"Who are His friends?", options:["Ye are my friends, if ye do whatsoever I command you.","All who hear my name.","All who claim my promises.","All who seek my blessings."], a:0, ref:"John 15:14",verse:"Ye are my friends, if ye do whatsoever I command you.",
   insight:"Friendship with Christ is not claimed by words but proved by obedience. Doing His will is the mark of His friends."},
  {q:"Why did Jesus call them friends instead of servants?", options:["For all things that I have heard of my Father I have made known unto you.","For they had forsaken all to follow Him.","For they had never doubted Him.","For they were chosen from Galilee."], a:0, ref:"John 15:15",verse:"Henceforth I call you not servants; for the servant knoweth not what his lord doeth: but I have called you friends; for all things that I have heard of my Father I have made known unto you.",
   insight:"A servant is not told the master's plans; a friend is. Jesus brought His followers into His confidence."},
  {q:"Who chose whom, according to Jesus?", options:["Ye have not chosen me, but I have chosen you.","Ye chose me when ye believed.","Ye and I chose one another.","The Father chose you, not I."], a:0, ref:"John 15:16",verse:"Ye have not chosen me, but I have chosen you, and ordained you, that ye should go and bring forth fruit, and that your fruit should remain: that whatsoever ye shall ask of the Father in my name, he may give it you.",
   insight:"Our choosing of Christ rests on His prior choosing of us. Grace began the friendship before we ever sought Him."},
  {q:"How did Jesus say the world would treat His disciples?", options:["If the world hate you, ye know that it hated me before it hated you.","The world will honor and reward you.","The world will leave you in peace.","The world will follow your teaching."], a:0, ref:"John 15:18",verse:"If the world hate you, ye know that it hated me before it hated you.",
   insight:"Hatred from the world is not a surprise; it is a sign we belong to Him. The world's hatred of Christ came first."},
  {q:"What saying did Jesus repeat about the servant?", options:["The servant is not greater than his lord.","The servant shall inherit the land.","The servant is free from duty.","The servant knows all the master's plans."], a:0, ref:"John 15:20",verse:"Remember the word that I said unto you, The servant is not greater than his lord. If they have persecuted me, they will also persecute you; if they have kept my saying, they will keep yours also.",
   insight:"If they persecuted Him, they will persecute us. We cannot expect kinder treatment than our Lord received."},
  {q:"Why would the world do these things to them?", options:["For my name's sake, because they know not him that sent me.","For their riches and lands.","For their rebellion against Rome.","For their breaking of the law."], a:0, ref:"John 15:21",verse:"But all these things will they do unto you for my name’s sake, because they know not him that sent me.",
   insight:"Persecution for Christ's name comes from not knowing the Father. The root of hostility is ignorance of God."},
  {q:"What will the Comforter do when He comes?", options:["He shall testify of me.","He shall condemn the world.","He shall write new scriptures.","He shall build the kingdom."], a:0, ref:"John 15:26",verse:"But when the Comforter is come, whom I will send unto you from the Father, even the Spirit of truth, which proceedeth from the Father, he shall testify of me:",
   insight:"The Spirit's great work is to point to Christ. Any spirit that does not testify of Jesus is not the Spirit of truth."}
 ]}
]);
